Mike Adams <MAdams@W3Link.com> wrote in article
<3408CC7C.751616E@W3Link.com>...
> HELP!
> 
> I am trying to convert an AlphaStation 200 4/233 that is running VMS to
> NT (which was originally on it).   I don't have access to the manuals
> for the system, and need to know the procedure to switch back to ARC
> console (which is loaded into flash), right now it comes up in the SRM
> console.   It seems like the solution had to do with setting the
> environment variable "boot_osflags"  but I am not sure...
> 
> I have done it before on this system but it has been a while, it is
> quite simple but just cannot find the commands online.  I need to get
> this system up right away and will not have access to the manuals for 4
> days...
> 
> 
> Thanx in advance..
> 
> 
> 
> --
> Michael L. Adams
> Director of Internet Technology
> DILAN, a Division of Pomeroy
> 

1. Insert the Firmware Update CD-Rom into the CD Drive.

2. Type the show device command to determine the device ID of the CD drive.

	>>>show device
	dka400.4.0.6.0		DKA400		TOSHIBA CD_ROM	0064

3. Boot Firmware Update Utility CD-ROM using the device ID display in step 2.

	>>>b -fl 0,a0 dka400

   You might need to know the correct path to the Bootfile.
   Apu->  prompt should come up.

4. To change to ARC console type:

	Apu-> update arc

5.  To verify the update:

	Apu-> verbose
	Apu-> verify

6.  If all okay, cycle the power (turn it off for 20 seconds).

     The ARC console should come up with power on.

Above name is alias.

Regards,

R.



