>  TSV05 might be MUA0 or MUB0...

Nope.  MSA0:, MSB0:, etc.  The TSV05 controller is TS11-emulating, remember.

>>I would like to reformat the drive and re-install the VMS software but
>>I don't know the syntax for VMS.
>
>  Do you have the DEC diagnostic floppies?  If so you can use them to format
>the disk.

Not if they're the "customer diagnostics".  At best, the customer
diagnostics will take an already-formatted hard drive and turn it
into an formatted hard drive.  Far more likely, though, is that the
customer diagnostics will destroy any formatting on the drive and
leave the drive in a severely screwed up partially or totally
unformatted state.

A far, far better choice for low-level-formatting a RD-series drive is
to do it on a VS2000 (has the formatting routine in firmware) or on
a PDP-11 with the XXDP diagnostics.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



