> have only 25% of memory available.  I thought I did not have enough
> swap, so I added a secondary swap, but the perfomance did not improve.
> Does anybody have any suggestions?

Secondary swap never improves perormance. It is better to make one
primary swap than primari + secondary. Secondary swap is a solution for
desperate situations, when you need more operative memory and have
primary swap and cannot (or are unwilling to) repartition system disc.

About your memory problem, how much memory did you have before?

It is possible for Digital UNIX to use more memory for some of it's
systems with more RAM. Actually, UBC (Unified Buffer Cache) does this.
It's quite possible that the figure you have is not tragic at all.

Nix.



