Your original values are not good if you have hardware problems during a
boot.  could end up with 3 single node clusters.

The safest way to do this is to use a quorum disk.  This has to be a
disk that all 3 systems have direct access too IE CI.  I would not think
that is your case.  However for completeness sake if you had that you
would set VOTES=1, EXPECTED_VOTES=6, DISK_QUORUM = "physical device
name",QDSKVOTES=3 on all 3 systems.  With these parameters any one
system and the quorum disk would form a running cluster.


Your other solution which has downsides is


VOTES=3, EXPECTED_VOTES=5 on the Alpha and
VOTES=1, EXPECTED_VOTES=5 on the Vaxes.  This REQUIRES the Alpha to be
running to have enough votes to survive as a cluster.

