Comp.sys.ultrix is probably the best place to ask DEC-station related
questions, but I happened to notice this.....


In article <5u2du7$gtu@overload.lbl.gov>, refling@comet.lbl.gov (Dr. John Refling) writes:
> 
> I want a decstation 5000/125 to boot using the ttya port as the
> console since I have an unsupported video card

> Any way to force this to use the serial port as the console?

Well, once you get to the console prompt( >>) prompt, do

  >> setenv console s

But your  problem is to get to the >> prompt in the first place, right?
You could try doing a shutdown -h a serial terminal, waiting long
enough for the system to halt, and then type the above on an LK-201
compatbile keyboard.

If all else fails, you can jumper the NVRAM to clear it out (as you
would do if you forgot the restricted-mode password), and then boot
without a framebuffer, keyboard, or mouse attached.


> (PMAG-C - ultimately
> I'm trying to get NetBSD to run on it). 

Oops. Note that NetBSD doesn't support the PMAG-C in any way, shape,
or form.  You will have to pull the board; the interrupt structure of
the 5000/1xx system is such that NetBSD can't yet safely ignore
unsupported TC devices (as NetBSD does on all other TC systems).

(See also the comments on the NetBSD Web page, requesting donations of
unsupported hardware in order to test drivers :)).



