This is a prompt for entering options.
You didn't mention if there are any disk drives, or what type they are.
Try 'B DU0' to boot the standard hard disk, It may be that they have
removed the hard disk drives, thus giving you the 'no such device' error.
Try 'B MU0' or 'B MS0' (depending on the type of tape drive) to boot from tape

