: instruct the machine to load from disk and ignore the hard drive. I
: have all the software on disk and could reformat the hard drive and
: load the system back on if that is the problem.

It's not clear what you mean you have "boot disks" being different from
the one "hard drive" you list.

You can boot the MVII off a particular device by specifying the device in the
boot command, for example:

>>> b dua0

Otherwize the MVII will search all disks (in controller order) all then any
ethernet devices.  There is no way to set the boot device like most VAXen.
If you do have other hard disks and one of them hasan OS, you may be best
off re-aranging the controller addresses so that the bootable disk is first.

