wade@dax.asub.arknet.edu writes:
> I have a VAX 4705 that I need more modem control serial ports in.
> I also have an old MVII with 2 M3104 serial controllers.  Is there
> any way these boards will work in the 4705.  It calls for the
> CXY08 board (that I don't have any spares)

  The M3104 is a DHV11 and is supported. The problem you're likely to have is
that you need S-handle cards in the 4705 to maintain FCC compliance. Also, the
"live" part of the Q-bus is the top half in the 4705, so if you have half-
height boards (I don't recall if the DHV11 is half- or full-height) it'll tend
to fall out from the weight of the cables.

  You can get CXY08's from many used equipment sellers. I recommend Compunet
at 800-767-9779 - ask for Tom Loonan and tell him Terry sent you. Be sure to
get the cables as well if you need 'em.

