George L. Schoenemann wrote:
> 
> >
> > Anyone have/know of a good replacement for this drive (include cost).
> > Want a 4mm DAT drive, would prefer either a TLZ07 or something
> > compatible with it, but am open to suggestions.
> > 
> I haven't priced one in a while, but that doesn't sound that out of line
> pricewise.  I hear the TLZ09 is very fast, but I'm sure it costs a bit
> more than the TLZ07.

Be careful, though. TLZ09 is a DDS2 drive and it can use both DDS and
DDS2 DATs. DDS2 cartridge is a 120m DAT, which can hold up to 4 GB of
uncompressed data.

What you should be careful about is DDS cartridge. We've had
difficulties with "less quality" DATs like BASF and SONY. The only one
we found satisfying was 3M (NO, THIS IS NOT AN ADVERTISMENT). All in
all, DDS2 drive is more sensitive to dust and "not quite the best" DDS
cartridges. Be warned.

Nix.



