X-Deja-AN: 265528375
Cache-Post-Path: demdwu29!unknown@193.189.230.163
Organization: Solutions for Media
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


We have an NT cluster using 5 disks in a StorageWorks array.

We have noticed that write performance seems to be very slow
using RAID 5 (we expected a bit slow, but not that slow).
The write performance of 1Mb/s was slower than using a single disk.

Using the writeback cache led to a speed of around 5Mb/s, which was
faster than the single disk. Indeed this was quite acceptable
performance.

However, using the cache seems to me to be a security hole. If the
system should ever go down without being able to flush the cache
then we would most likely end up with some kind of corruption,
especially as we wish to run a database system on the cluster.

How safe is the write-back cache mechanism and what are reasonable
write rates to expect ?

Does anyone have any ideas,
     best regards,
           Russell



