In article <33FADDB1.7A6A7644@euro.apple.com>, Mark Alexander Sovereign <sovereign.m@euro.apple.com> writes:
>
>1.  4Gb disk drives at the last time i was building alpha systems were
>not able to go internally to 2100 machines as in external storage ba3.XX
>they need the twin speed fans for cooling. So this disk will have to go
>external.

We have a 4Gb drive in our 2100 in an interal StorageWorks shelf.  When we
talked to DEC about this they went back and forth and finally pulled up the
relevant info.  The twin speed fans are for EXTERNAL storageworks shelves,
the ones inside the 2100, at least the older model we have (190 Mhz) depend
on the windtunnel like draft built up by the big fans built into the 2100's
chassis, and if I remember right, don't even have their own fans. Word from
DEC was that there is sufficient ventilation for the 4 Gb disks inside.  Of
course, we have just one such disk.  I'm not sure what happens if you pack
up both StorageWorks shelf with them.

>2. Depending which controller cards you may have two or one bus for both
>the internal shelfs dka, dkb or dka100, dka200 etc.

Each internal shelf can be wired to be two buses, or one buses, depending 
on how the jumpers on the back are set.  So you can have as many as 4 
internal SCSI buses running in the two Storageworks shelves.  Currently we
have 3 SCSI controllers (the built in, an EISA, and the PCI card model
(KZPAA)).  The built in and PCI controllers are functionally identical: one
controls all of the disks in the single shelf (wired as a bus), the other
controls the two CDROM drives and feeds out the back to an external TZ87. 
The EISA controller runs a bunch of older disks, all external. 

>
>3. SCSI lengths are for normal max. of 9 feet 3m approx.
>    SCSI2 fast and wide this can go to 9 meters /27 feet make sure you
>have the correct cable and personality modules if this option is used.
>Ive been caught how by this one.

Yes, you do have 3 meters of cable for the Fast SCSI-2 buses, but the
internal cables for the 2100 from DEC are 2.25 meters.  That leaves a grand
total of .75 meters for anything outside the case.  The built in SCSI
connector is about an inch below the top of the case, so pretty much you
have to put the next SCSI device right on top of the 2100 box or the cable
to reach it will be too long.  If one of the SCSI controllers is driving an 
internal Storageworks shelf you don't have enough cable length to attach an 
external device on that bus (section 3-34 of our 2100 manual.)  There are 
all sorts of other caveats. For instance, even if the SCSI doesn't go into
an internal storageworks shelf, the built in SCSI only allows 1.5 meters of
external cable.  If anyone is planning to have tons of disks, look into the 
differential SCSI controllers - they give you enough length to place 
external disks conveniently.

Regards,

