As a last resort, you could create a "Code Load Tape" with the
8200(low-density) as a default. Of 'cause, you should have a "normal"
code load tape. The when you need a 8200, you just load firmware
via this tape, and when finished with 8200 tapes, reload the normal 8500 setup.

