Todd Wallace wrote:
> 
> I am adding a 4 gig external hard drive to my AlphaServer 2100 4/233.
> I have already ordered this unit from our DEC supplier, but I want to
> install it myself.
> 
> Question: Do I need to open up the Alpha to pull a terminator, or do I
> even have to worry about terminators?

You might, it depends on the controller.  Some of the newer controllers
auto-terminate, but the older controllers have a jumper that you'll have
to remove.  Make sure you have a terminator on the internal drive end
(should already be there) and at the end of your new external cable.

Otherwise, just be sure that your total SCSI cable length is within
limits.  That ribbon cable that snakes around the inside of that 2100
can be longer than you think.  I believe that the cable supplied with
the 2100 for the secondary controllers is about 3 feet long, so it eats
up a third of your maximum length all by itself.

