X-Deja-AN: 264952370
References: <qxpvi152mva.fsf@foobar.cs.colorado.edu>
Organization: University of Colorado
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec




The problem is that the program uses '%lld' to specify the printing of
a 'long long', or the scanning of a long long.

Someone suggested writing a converter that would check & convert the
strings on the fly. E.g,

	fprintf(stderr,CleanMeUp("i always say woof a%lld ay log"), my_data)

Another alternative is to use pre-processoror string concatenation.

Yet another was to link with the Gnu libc routines, which correctly handle this case.

-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



