Well, as far as I can determine, neither Intel nor Digital have posted
info on Pentium Overdrive compatiblity for the Starion 300i (75 mHz
Pentium)....so I thought I would relate my experience here.

Since the 300i motherboard has settings for 75, 90 and 100 mHz (and
the factory default is 90 mHz), I've always figured the 150 mHz
Overdrive intended for P90s should work OK.  Well, I just picked one
up cheap ($126) and popped it in...and the system registers it as a
120 mHz cpu...and Intel's diagnostic software thinks it's a P125!  I
guess I may as well have bought the proper 75 --> 125 mHz Overdrive
instead.

Oh, well, at least it works.  Maybe switching the motherboard to 100
mHz will boost it up to the P150 level where it's supposed to be, but
I'll probably just leave it be...unless anybody else has some info on
this to share.

Dave



