> I have an LPS17 printer that I want to print to from unix and other
> systems. To do this I want to set up an lpr queue.
> I am currently using DCPS to run a normal VMS print que.  From what I
> have read it is not possible to use DCPS to run an LPD que.

You can set up an LPR queue pointing to the DCPS one, and share the LPR
queue to other systems.  All remote Unix jobs then use the DCPS queue,
which in turn uses either DECnet or TCP/IP to print to the printer.

> Unfortunately the DECNET and IP names are not the same which confuses
> things slightly I am assuming I should use the ip address for rm: I am
> not clear what if anything rp should be.

If you want to set up an LPR queue directly to the printer (you don't
have to), use the TCP/IP name or address for rm, and anything you want
for rp.

