In article <33f479dd.420557830@news.boeing.com>,
 <kyrrin@wizards.DIE_SPAM_DIE.net> wrote:
>Hi, folks,
>
>	Got a DEC TZ30 tape drive. 5.25" half-height, SCSI interface,
>appears to take the same physical type of cartridge as a TK50.
>However, I suspect that it is of much later vintage and may be able to
>handle CompacTape II.

It will handle physical CompacTape II cartridges, but will only be
able to read/write TK50 (95 MByte/cart) format on them.  It will
not read or write TK70 format, if this is what you're asking.

CompacTape II carts with a TK70 format on them will almost certainly
need to be bulk degaussed before use in a TZ30/TK50.

>	Any info on this drive, including jumper settings and what
>system(s) it was intended to work with, would be much appreciated.

It came with several desktop systems, including various VaxStation 3100
models.  The actuall TZ30 mechanism is made by Sony.

Tim.



