Perhaps the greatest coup of the notorious Chas. Matco was the
revelation of the Epoxy Backplane Scam. Back in the days of the
VAXstation II, DEC created a low-cost restricted configuration
VAXstation called, not surprisingly, the VAXstation II RC (for
Restricted Configuration). The configuration was restricted by
filling several of the backplane slots with epoxy cement. When
Matco was tipped off (by an RSX UFO-ologist whose wife's name is
Sharon), he included the tidbit in his column. You'd be amazed
at how many replacement backplanes were sold by third-party DEC
component dealers! Digital was not amused.

