> 
> The uname -a says: OSF1 shiva.baltimore.oxmol.com V4.0 564 alpha

Has the drive ever worked?

I have a TLZ09 connected to an AlphaStation 255/300 which is running OpenVMS.
The drive worked perfectly for about a month, then suddenly failed.  Every
attempt to use it with data compression turned on resulted in lots of R/W
errors.  If I turned off data compression it worked OK.

So I put in a call to DEC and it was replaced.

The DEC technician and I both observed that the failed drive was rather
warm and he suspected the fan had failed.  Upon closer inspection of the
rear of the unit he came to the conclusion there wasn't a fan installed! 
The new one appears to have a fan (albeit not very powerful) and the
external markings indicate it's a later hardware revision ... so maybe
they discovered a fan was necessary after all.

