			--------------------
			X M C D  version 2.2
			--------------------
			     by Ti Kan

I am pleased to announce the release of xmcd version 2.2, a package
including xmcd, an X11/Motif-based CD player utility and cda, a
command-line driven, non-graphical CD audio player.

In its evolution over the past few years, xmcd has established itself
as the premier CD player application for the X window system with an
attractive, easy-to-use user interface.  It is feature-rich and runs on
virtually all of the popular UNIX and OpenVMS platforms.  It also
supports the widest array of CD-ROM and CD-R devices, including some
older SCSI-1 drives that do not work with other CD player applications.
The remote CD database query feature fully utilizes the Internet and
taps on a vast repository of CD artists/titles, track titles and other
information.

Version 2.2 adds multi-disc changer support, HTTP support for
remote CD database access, proxy server support, more OS and system
platforms, more CD-ROM drives, plus much more!

Please visit the xmcd web page for full information, screen snapshot
and downloads:

    http://sunsite.unc.edu/~cddb/xmcd/

If you don't have web access, xmcd can also be obtained via
anoymous FTP.  Please e-mail xmcd@amb.org for information.

