Start Unit is Start Unit. If the drive won't spin up, it's toast.
It's only a 200MB or so drive, so it's not a huge loss.

Wait Spin would be to cause it to wait a certain amount of time after
Start Unit before spinning up. Usually, this woul be the 1 second, times
the SCSI ID, thus SCSI ID 2 is 2 seconds after Start Unit and SCSI ID 5 is
5 seconds after Start Unit.

Possibly, the drive is experiencing stiction, you could give it a sharp
wrap with your knuckles and it might spin up. I wouldn't count on it
lasting for ever though.

