On Thu, 14 Aug 1997, jpg wrote:
> I do not know much about 32/64bit and x86/Alpha RISC instructions,
> so could someone please explain when Intel finaly go 64bit and drop
> the x86 instruction processors (NT is going 64 bit)  and software
> manufactures start producing software for the new Intel chips, will
> these apps work on existing 21164/21264 processors and motherboards
> as if they were ported for Alpha, or will their be a new ver. of
> FX!32 type emulation software, or am I off track ???

  Code written for the new IA64 architecture (what Intel was calling the x86
replacement, last I heard) will not run on Intel x86 chips, nor will it run on
Alpha CPUs.  They use different instruction sets, and different subsystem
designs.  Existing x86 will be runnable on IA64 in an "emulation mode", the
exact details of which aren't exactly clear yet.  As to whether Digital
can/will come up with an IA64 emulator for the Alpha, no one knows at this
point. 

  Hope this helps.

