the wharf rat wrote:
> 
>         Can you cluster Alpha NT systems the way you used to do with
> VAXen?

No. (But...)

You can get that kind of clustering on Alphas, but not under NT - you 
need OpenVMS for full-featured clustering, or DIGITAL Unix for stable 
shared storage, load balancing, and so forth.

However, if you're willing to settle for application failover, there
is "DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT," which runs on Alphas and
provides failover capabilities for selected applications with shared 
SCSI storage. 

Over time, expect clustering to improve - it's a hot area for
DEC (and plenty of other companies), especially with Microsoft's 
recent attempts to push into the enterprise computing arena. For
now, if you need to get the most reliability NT can provide,
you can add "cluster" failover capabilities to your toolkit.

