In article <33F49CAD.73D5@gist.net.au>, aek <aek@gist.net.au> writes:
:  I'm seeking information on talking to a VT340 graphix terminal.

  The VT340 is a color graphic terminal supporting various character
  sets including ASCII, and various graphics protocols including ReGIS.
  There are three manuals -- Installing and Using, Text Programming,
  and Graphics Programming -- that cover this particular terminal in
  some detail.

  This terminal is largely a superset of earlier VT-series terminals.

  If you are expecting to do graphics programming with this terminal,
  you will need the abovementioned manuals and/or you will need the
  documentation for the particular package or library you are using
  as a display manager for the terminal.

  The order number for the documentation kit is EK-VT3XX-UP.  The
  folks at 1-800-DIGITAL should be able to get you this.

  For listings of common escape sequences, look in /etc/termcap or in
  sys$system:smgterms.txt on UNIX or OpenVMS, respectively.  (These
  areas are not a complete list, and will likely lack most of (all of?)
  the graphics sequences you will need for graphics programming.

