We had a beutiful problem once. We had aprox. 100 pty devices and
Digital UNIX was unable to open more than 16 sessions on telnet. What
was the joke about?

Your terminal device drivers (device special files) start frop
ttyp0/ptyp0 to ttypf/ptypf. For 17-th telnet connection UNIX wants
ttyq0!!! In other words, they MUST be in a continous line, from 0 to f,
from p to q, from q to r and so on.

Could this be your problem?

