rbarris@netcom.com (Robert Barris) writes:
>What is the freq of visible light in GHz or THz anyway?

Light travels about 3e8 meters/sec.  Visible light has a wavelength of
from about .4 to .7 micron, and f=c/lambda.  For red light that is
3e8/0.7e-6, or about 4.3e14 Hz or 430 THz.  Violet would be 750 THz.

1 GHz is a wavelength of 0.3 meters, about 1 foot, so we could still deal
with that.  Life changes drastically when the wavelength of your clock
frequency is no longer much bigger than your chip width, since you can't
build a synchronous circuit any more.





