In article <5snjke$glo$1@news.wizvax.net>, weber@wizvax.net (michael weber) writes:
:I have been working trying to get a Vaxstation II GPX to boot.  It
:goes through the hardware test, but then gives a ?54 error when
:loading the operating software.  Does anyone know what this error code
:is and, more importantly, how to correct it?

  ?54 RETRY (or some such similar text) typically indicates that the
  console PROM has likely passed self-test, and that it has tried to
  locate a copy of OpenVMS VAX around on a local disk or tape, and has
  not succeeded, and is now sending MOP requests, asking for a network
  downline load.  Each download request retry generates, you guessed it.

  Failures on the hard disk usually result in messages other than ?54.

  You will likely need to acquire a copy of standalone BACKUP on TK50,
  and a copy of an OpenVMS distribution (hobbyist OpenVMS VAX V6.1 is
  available at http://www.montagar.com, non-hobbyist kits are available
  from the folks at 1-800-DIGITAL), and install OpenVMS VAX on your
  local system disk.

  You will also need a DECwindows Motif kit, as well as licenses for
  OpenVMS and Motif.

  Insert the standalone BACKUP TU58 into the TK50 drive:

	>>> B MUA0
	...
	... swap to the distribution TK50, if the distribution
	... is on a volume other than the standalone BACKUP kit...
	SAB$ BACKUP MUA0:VMS061.B/SAVE/REWIND DUA0:/IMAGE/VERIFY
	...
	SAB$
	<BREAK>
	>>> B DUA0
	...

