Unless my memory is slipping the ra series drives have two plugs on the rear.
One is for input A and the other is for input B. These two ports are so the
drive can be connected to to seperate systems or seperate controllers on an HSC.
It is important that the A and/or B button on the front panel be pushed in. If
the appropriate button is not depressed then any controller/system on that
channel can not access that drive.

The RA controller on the system end has 4 connections one for each possible
drive that it can access. It should matter which port you use at the system end.

Lastly the RA ID plug was a bunch of binary weighted tabs on the back. The unit
number is selected by breaking off tabs. The tabs should be labelled so you
should be able to figure out the real ID.

Good Luck

Brian V

