   If you insert the recovery diskette and install J10, when you start
the system, the screen will be blank. After some period of time, the
system will start to beep - this is the same set of beeps that you heard
during Phlash. I believe that there are about 20-30 beeps. There are two
sets of beeps that you should hear - the first set is while the BIOS is
being cleared, the second set is while the new BIOS is being written.
This process takes about 3-5 minutes. When the second set of beeps are
complete, you should then hear another set of beeps, about 2 or 3. This
indicates that the Phlash is complete.

If this still does not work, you'll have to call Digital service.

