>Yes, but there were two more connectors labeled "IN" and "OUT."  These
>were for spin-up sequencing to prevent more than one drive from spinning
>up at a time and popping the circuit breaker in a 3 or 4 drive rack.
>
>A cable ran from the "OUT" on the top drive to "IN" on the next one
>down, and so on to the bottom drive which had a terminator in the "OUT"
>connector.  The "IN" connector on the top drive was left open.  A single
>drive configuration consists of nothing more than a terminator in the
