Don,

Which DEC466dx2?  Does it take 30-pin or 72-pin SIMMs?  Do you have
any unused SIMM sockets?

As a rule, the older DEC PCs used parity memory.  Many of the older
ones will not accept the "two-sided" 8MB SIMMs.

Strictly a wild guess, but you probably can add either 2 4MB 1x36 or 2
16MB 4x36 72-pin SIMMs.  And most 486s are happy if the SIMMs are not
added in pairs, but singly... Ben 

