In article <19970808204301.QAA28536@ladder02.news.aol.com>, beerisfree@aol.com (Beerisfree) writes:

:..When I start my [HiNote VP model ???] computer a red
:flashing screen shows up saying that my partition is corrupted or disabled
:and save to disk feature is disabled. I've talked to a lot of people about
:it and one person told me to download a new bios driver, flash the bios. I
:was wondering where to find it for this pirticular laptop.

  This has nothing to do with the BIOS.

  Most (all?) HiNote BIOS and drivers are available at the DIGITAL website.
  Be *sure* you download and use the *correct* BIOS for the *specific* "VP"
  model in use, as several systems share the "VP" designation.

:If this sounds right or if you have another option pealse tell me. 

  You will have to repartition the drive, as the save-to-disk partition
  is apparently corrupt.  There is a disk partition of around 42 MB
  specifically set aside for the save-to-disk operation, and phdisk is
  used to work with this partition.  (The phdisk tool is included with
  the utilities and tools provided with/for this system.)

  You'll probably end up repartitioning your drive, and reloading.  (Make
  sure you have your software backed up, obviously.)

