Hum...  Neither NT nor Digital UNIX can access the disk...  That's
probably the problem.  Whether it is a problem specific to that disk
or to that family of disk I don't know.  But you need to find out
why.  I don't know if the standalone system of Digital UNIX has
the tools to look at the error log and you need those to see what
the error is.  You might be better off seeing what you can do from
NT to get the disk working and to see what the errors are.

I think the standalone system has scu(8) on it.  That will let
you do a Test Unit Ready and some basic media check commands.
If those don't work, scu(8) may offer a clue why.

