Quite true. However, you'll never see Digital sell OVMS as cheaply as
they sell WNT. DEC pays Micro$oft about $600 for each WNT-based system
it ships (e.g. $600 for the NTAS license), and that represents the vast
majority of DEC's costs. Being as OVMS belongs to DEC, DEC is
responsible for the care and feeding of the OS (ongoing development,
maintenance, etc).

Reducing the cost of enterprise-class OVMS licenses to NTAS levels would
not be in DEC's best interests.

