Bruce Lane wrote:
> 
> Fellow DEC'ers...
> 
>         I have need of a utility that will let me read/write RX50 disks,
> initialized with MicroVMS 4.6, on a PC. I've tried RX50.EXE (the archive)
> and PUTR already; neither work.
> 
>         Formatting capability is not necessary. I can already initialize with
> the VAXen.
> 
>         Please E-mail replies. Don't forget to de-munge my address (remove the
> DIE_SPAM_DIE) portion or it'll bounce.

I don't know of such utilities. All the RX50 floppy "drivers" for PCs
that I know of (RAINDOS, RX50) are for handling Rainbow formatted (i.e.,
MS-DOS) floppies.

PATHWORKS (starting from V2.0 or thereabouts - which should work for VMS
4.6)
included a utility called PCDISK to create PC format (FAT) diskettes on
a VAX system (it won't work with Alpha, or at least didn't use to when I
last
saw it).

PATHWORKS of the VMS 4.6 era was known as "VAX/VMS Services for PCs" (or
something very close to that). It was also often referred to as "PCSA"
(which meant Personal Computing Systems Architecture). The PATHWORKS
name
came about around V3.0 (or just after it; I don't remember for sure any
longer).

Also, someone in PATHWORKS engineering did build a kit with PCDISK only,
which could be distributed and used provided you had a license to run
PATHWORKS (which in the V4/V5 time meant that a $99 client access
license
was enough; in the V2/V3 timeframe the server software license was for
a while bundled with DECnet-VAX, and before that it was a separate,
relatively expensive license).

regards,
