Fred Kleinsorge (kleinsorge@star.enet.dec.com) wrote:

[ snip ]

:   Are your demos doing anything that would tend to keep the system in
:   a COM state?  

The demos are running a large optimization package, which keeps the
system in the COM state.

:   Can they be modified to allow some idle time?

Good question - I'll ask the developers to see what they can come up
with, perhaps based on a logical name.

: As part of the idle loop on the Tadpole, the CPU speed is dropped,
: when it leaves the idle loop, it is raised.  The CPU will eventually
: overheat if it runs at full speed too long, and then the speed is 
: reduced to let it cool, and reduced again if the temperature continues 
: to rise (which it will, if the CPU remains in a COM state).  The lowest 
: speed will allow the CPU to cool even if the system remains in a COM state.

: I've considered adding logic to the graphics driver to slow the CPU
: speed when the screen saver activates (it would, of course, need to be
: optional).

: The case is a heat sink, so I imagine that if you were to make a large
: thick aluminum plate with fins on the bottom, and possibly a small DC
: fan to push air through them - it would help to cool the box.  You
: need to make sure that the plate makes the best possible fit with the
: bottom to conduct as much heat as possible.

Thanks,

