<alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com> wrote in article <5sdasn$2lf@nntpd2.cxo.dec.com>...
> 
> If the disk is well behaved you don't a disktab entry.  The
> disklabel command can get the geometry from the drive and
> the default partition table from the driver.  Since it sounds
> like you don't want to partition it, just use the C partition.
> 
> 1.  Connect the disk.  If you need to unterminate the bus to
>     add the disk it would be wise to shutdown.
> 
> 2.  Verify the console can see the disk.  This will also
>     let you collect the bus and target ID.
> 
> 3.  Boot.
> 
> 4.  Create the special files:
> 
> 	# cd /dev
> 	# ./MAKEDEV rz#
> 
>     where the '#' in rz# is (bus * 8) + target-id.  On systems
>     with a single bus, the bus number is zero.
> 
> 5.  Label the disk:
> 
> 	# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c whatever
> 
> 6.  Create the file system and mount:
> 
> 	# newfs /dev/rrz#c
> 	# mount /dev/rz#c /wherever
> --
> Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




