> and I can't boot the machine because one of the RA81 terminators is
> missing.  I have plenty of resistors around, can I make one?

If you're talking about the sequence IN/OUT terminator: As far as I know, 
this so called "Terminator" is not a resistor like the 50 Ohm terinators 
for the ethernet cable.

This terminator for the sequence IN/OUT lines is only a single cable
which closes the sequence chain as far as I can remember. So 
if you know the pin-out of the sequence connector you could just
stick a belted wire into the contacts to get it going.

