In article <33ee0dd8.3527602@news.wizards.net>,
Bruce Lane <kyrrin@wizards.DEATH_TO_SPAM.net> wrote:
>	I have need of a utility that will let me read/write RX50 disks,
>initialized with MicroVMS 4.6, on a PC. I've tried RX50.EXE (the archive)
>and PUTR already; neither work.

I assure you PUTR *does* work, but it does not yet have support for ODS-1
or ODS-2 file systems.  It has good RT-11 support though, so if you can't
find a utility with built-in ODS support, you can use VMS EXCHANGE to
access RT-11 format disks which will interchange fine with PUTR.

If PUTR's RT-11 support doesn't work for you, PLEASE drop me a line and
describe the problem so I can fix it.  I've put way too much work into
PUTR to tolerate bugs, it's not as if it's some quick-and-dirty junk that
I don't care about!

BTW there is a known problem (found and diagnosed by Tim Shoppa) with PUTR
and VMS EXCHANGE RT-11 disks which prevents PUTR from auto-detecting the disk
format if the disk was initialized by EXCHANGE, so you must use the "/RT11"
switch on PUTR's MOUNT command line with such disks.  It seems EXCHANGE puts
its own signature in the home block instead of the standard RT-11 signature;
naturally I find it convenient to consider this a bug in EXCHANGE, not PUTR,
but anyway the upcoming version of PUTR will recognize the DECVMSEXCHNG
signature as well as the DECRT11A one so we can all just get along...

