In article <01bca29c$b32e86e0$d586f1c3@boldy>, "Boldy" <Boldy@dds.nl> writes:
:I need a console cable for the MicroVax II. I tried a cable with shorted 8
:and 9 pin but is didn't work!!! What can be wrong?

  The MicroVAX and VAXstation 2000 shorted a set of pins in the
  connector to indicate the presence of the console line -- other
  MicroVAX and VAX system consoles did not use this scheme.  (If
  memory serves, that cable was the BCC05.)

:Can someone tell me where to order a BCC08 Cable ?

  The OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) has the necessary
  DECconnect adapter part numbers for this task -- order the correct
  DB9-MMJ adapter, some BC16E MMJ wiring, and the appropriate MMJ-DB25
  adapter for your specific requirement(s).  1-800-DIGITAL.  String
  it together, and you're in business -- the modular wiring is very
  easy to deal with, uses interchangeable components, and tends to be
  more convenient than the older cabling system.  (It does not "do"
  modems, however.)

    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms
    ftp://rtfm.mit.edu/pub/usenet/news.answers/dec-faq/vms

