In article <33E5F829.3DE8F935@mci.com>, Timothy Lee Couger <tim.couger@mci.com> writes:
|> > I'm trying to figure out what the ephemeral port range is for DEC Unix.
|> > On HPUX (and BSD?) it is 1025-5000.  On Solaris, I believe it is
|> > everything above 32768.
|> 
|> Found my answer ...
|> 
|> This information is defined in the <netinet/in.h> header file.  In this
|> file you will find the following comment:
|> 
|> #define IPPORT_USERRESERVED     5000

This is now a configurable parameter for Digital UNIX.  According
to
   http://www.digital.com/info/internet/document/ias/tuning.html

     You can set this parameter on DIGITAL UNIX Versions 3.2G, 4.0A, or
     higher, or on the patched version of DIGITAL UNIX V3.2C or higher.
     This parameter is not available on Version 4.0.

The maximum value is 65535; the default is still 5000.

-Jeff



