Robert Lopez wrote:
> 
> I am unable to open a shared folder on the alpha server using a NT 4.0
> workstation.  However,  I can open the shared directory using another
> server...any solutions out there???  Thank you in advance!!

Check share permissions first, file/directory permissions second.

Without more information it is impossible to say more.

If that doesn't help, then go back and find out:

    What are the share permissions?

    What are the permissions for the directories from the root
    down to where you're trying to get?

    What are the permissions of the files in the directory
    the share points to?

    Is the workstation a member of the domain or workgroup
    the server is in?

    What is the role of the server in the domain?

    Does it have a connection to the domains' primary
    or backup domain controller?

    Are you logged on as a local user or a domain user
    on the workstation?

    Does the account have any access restrictions?

    Is the workstation on the same LAN as the server?

    Can you access other resources on the server from
    the workstation, or is it just this one share that
    fails?

    What, exactly, did you attempt to do?

    What, exactly (including any and all exact error
    messages) happened?

    If you tried to access the share with Explorer,
    is it any different if you try to map a drive
    to it with "NET USE d: \\server\share /user:domain\username"?

    Why are you asking in comp.sys.dec instead of
    a newsgroup about Windows NT (see, e.g., Microsoft's
    NNTP server msnews.microsoft.com)?

    Did you think this was somehow an Alpha-specific
    problem instead of just an NT system managemenr,
    networking type of issue?

    If so, why?

    Etc., etc.

