  I'm sure you have an understanding of the [in]famous question poised every
  year by each new legion of undergraduate computer science students: "why
  doesn't my program work?"  :-)  And without further information, the only
  honest answer can be: "because there is something wrong."

  There is nowhere near enough information included in your posting -- you
  do not include critical information such as the model of Alpha system and
  the configuration, operating system and version, as well as a large amount
  of other information critical to answering this or similar performance-
  related questions.

  Once the baseline hardware and storage configuration is understood, and
  once baseline statistics for the application are available, then one can
  begin to determine where the hotspots are, and how to remove them -- this
  is "tuning 101" -- and to look at potential programming tweaks, at any
  preprocessors, at system and storage configuration, and/or at basic
  programming design strategies and changes...

