>I once heard someone say that a 500MHz Alpha CPU is equivalent to a 100MHz
>Intel Pentium (kind of like how an AMD 5x86 is like an i486).  Is this
>true?

True in the sense that if you run SoftWindows (pure software emulator
of x86 architecture) the results are likely to approximate a 100MHz x86
chip. In the sense of actual CPU performance doing equivalent stuff
using its own code, not so at all. Not even close.

Be aware though that the x86 instruction set is doomed; next generation
Intel will start using IA64 which will NOT be compatible (save in the
sense of a compat mode).



