ByteMark is using a Dell Pentium 90, as index.
I just ran these bytemarks on my 600MHz Alpha, and came up with these
results:

Integer Index:             8.47
Floating-Point Index:     10.10
--------------------------------

The ByteMark test only uses processor and memory for the purpose, and 
therefore gives a pretty good indication of raw processor power.

I've also tested Protels AutoRouter(x86 binaries), running under FX!32,
against a 200MHz PPro, which gave me following routing times:


           PPro             Alpha/FX!32
Board 1:   9 sek.           7 sek.
Board 2:   2min 36sek       2min 13sek.
Board 3:   6min 32sek       5min 35sek.
Board 4    11min 14sek      8min 53sek.

Both computers are equipped with 128MB RAM, and running NT4.0.

for what it's worth

