Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Timothy Lee Couger wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to figure out what the ephemeral port range is for DEC Unix.
> On HPUX (and BSD?) it is 1025-5000.  On Solaris, I believe it is
> everything above 32768.
> 
> Thanks for any info provided ...
> 

Found my answer ...

This information is defined in the <netinet/in.h> header file.  In this
file you will find the following comment:

/*
 * Local port number conventions:
 * Ports < IPPORT_RESERVED are reserved for
 * privileged processes (e.g. root).
 * Ports > IPPORT_USERRESERVED are reserved
 * for servers, not necessarily privileged.
 */
#define IPPORT_RESERVED         1024
#define IPPORT_USERRESERVED     5000

I interprete this as saying that ports 1-1023 are the well known ports,
ports 1024-5000 are the ephermal ports, and port 5001 through 65535 are
for the non-priveledge server (user defined) ports.

