It's a known situation.
1. Set MPU I/O address in CMOS (under INTEGRATED PERIPHERAL) to
     320 and use the same address (320) in the DRIVER INSTALLATION.

2. Set the CAPTURE IRQ (in the driver) to 5.

If this fails to correct the problem, you may need to
vary the address and/or IRQ.




