In article <33e1079c.0@news.cloudnet.com>, rossib <rossib@cloudnet.com> wrote:
>
>ya..  You missed the part that says "If you run linux you won't have any
>of these lame problems".

That's because that part really says, `if you run Linux you'll have
rabid Linuxers giving you incorrect information.'

>You can easily load winNT and Linux, Ultrix from
>the Linux Loader LILO.

Ultrix? You have a MIPS emulator for your Alpha? I'll assume you
were talking about Digital Unix.

First of all, you want to use MILO, the Alpha boot loader; LILO is
the i386 boot loader. Second, you need to have NT PALcode (which
generally comeswith the ARC console) to run NT, and you must have
OSF PALcode (which generally comes with the SRM console) to run
Digital Unix. Linux uses its own PALcode which is contained in MILO
(which is why any particular build of MILO will boot only one
particular model of machine), so MILO can be loaded from either
the ARC or the SRM consoles, or written into flash memory if you
don't want a console.

So while Linux will boot on a supported machine regardless of
console, it doesn't help to run other operating systems at all.

