PRISM was a scalar/vector architecture. DEC elected to scuttle PRISM on
March 26, 1988 (or thereabouts) and begin work on a superscalar
architecture whilst using MIPS as a stopgap. This could have been
because...

A) There was no software for PRISM (problems with the VMS-like MICA OS)

B) You only derive benefits from vectors when an application is >98
percent vectorizable.

C) DEC didn't do too well with the vector coprocessors on Calypso

D) DEC realized that IBM was on the right track with POWER architecture.


