peterm@landau.EECS.Berkeley.EDU (Peter Mardahl) writes:
> It's possible someone could contrive some bizarre measure by which
> a 500MHz 21164A Alpha was slower than a 100MHz Pentium P5, but
> they would have to try hard.
> 
> In SpecInt95, a 500MHz 21164A system is about 5 times faster than 
> a 100MHz P5, and
> in SpecFP95, a 500MHz 21164A system is about 8 times faster than a
> 100MHz P5.
> 
> Ergo, a 500MHz alpha is > 5x faster than a 100MHz pentium, at
> least on SPEC benchmarks.  The numbers to back me up
> are on www.specbench.org.
> 

Note that these numbers are not apples to apples comparisons.  The
SPEC numbers rate systems, not just CPUs, and the numbers I think you
are citing for the Alpha are on systems with much better memory
systems than the P5 has. Comparing CPU<->CPU would require comparing
systems with similar motherboards, etc. OTOH, if you did this
comparison, a 500MHz Alpha would be significantly faster than a 100MHz
P5.

