Im running OSF 4.0 and Im having problems with core files in a 
multithreaded program.
If I catch the signals and then call abort this is what I get..


(gdb) where
#0  0x3ff800d4620 in _sigprocmask ()
#1  0x3ff800d6964 in sigprocmask ()
#2  0x3ff80170aec in abort ()
#3  0x3ff80565b08 in errAbort ()
#4  0x3ff8056639c in excInit ()
#5  0x3ff807b2210 in exc_set_last_chance_handler ()
warning: Hit heuristic-fence-post without finding
warning: enclosing function for address 0x2001befc00038d60
This warning occurs if you are debugging a function without any symbols
(for example, in a stripped executable).  In that case, you may wish to
increase the size of the search with the `set heuristic-fence-post' command.

Otherwise, you told GDB there was a function where there isn't one, or
(more likely) you have encountered a bug in GDB.


And yes its compiled with symbols.

