The early PC XLs that have two sockets and one jumper for clock speed
(60/66) won't upgrade to anything other than 100 Mhz and one processor. The
two-jumper/two-socket daughtercard will upgrade to dual 133s (jumper for
3/2 & 2X). The dual 200 capable card was a later Celebris XL, three jumper
daughtercard (2 jumpers for 3/2,2,5/2,3X) 
There exists a DECpc XL to Celebris 6150 (Pentium Pro) powergrade - that
daughterboard clocks up to 366 (yeh right :-)). I've heard rumour of a dual
PPro but have never seen one - the reference is from DEC sales claiming
that the XL would be upgradeable to dual Pros - don't think they ever made
the card.
 
But. . . I upgraded my Celebris XL 590 with the 6150 kit - it didn't work -
and it's been at DEC PC repair since 27 June (Celebris XL hostage crisis -
Day 40).

